# Your Problem-Solving Rule

This is probably the most important part of the entire plan.

When you encounter a problem:

### Step 1 — Understand

Spend 5 minutes making sure you understand the input/output.

### Step 2 — Brute force

Ask:

> "If I didn't care about efficiency, how would I solve this?"

### Step 3 — Write it down

Literally write pseudocode.

### Step 4 — Code

Try for **20–30 minutes**.

### Step 5 — Get unstuck

If you're genuinely stuck, look at a **hint**, not the entire solution.

### Step 6 — Study the solution

If you still can't solve it, read the solution carefully.

### Step 7 — Close it

Then rewrite the solution **without looking**.

### Step 8 — Revisit

Solve the same problem again **2–3 days later**.

That last step is where a lot of your actual learning will happen.

