## One more thing: keep a DSA notebook

For every problem you fail to solve, record just four things:

```text
Problem:
My approach:
Where I got stuck:
What I learned:
```

Don't write pages of notes.

For example:

```text
Problem: Reverse Linked List

My approach:
Tried changing current.next directly.

Where I got stuck:
Lost reference to the rest of the list.

What I learned:
Save next before changing current.next.
Use previous/current/next.
```

When you review this two weeks later, you'll see exactly how your problem-solving is improving.

